Indeed. There are at least a couple of wand types that deserve being
identified to know their charges; all the escape/defense wands. In my
list are (priority 1) teleportation, digging, fire, lightning, sleep,
death, polymorph. Mind that fire and lightning are meant as defense
wands to write the E-word (or burn away green slime with fire) not to
zap at monsters (in this case), sleep to get the time to flee not to
fight it and wake it up again (in this case), and death because it's
the only guaranteed on-shot-attack measure (*if* it hits) against a
row of monsters. Polymorph is of course lowest priority, mainly because
it's gamling und unreliable but occasionally worthwhile if none of the
other wands are available, and it's best used from distance, anyway.

